ages in the advancement of observability for digital businesses, which transforms the complexity of modern digital ecosystems in North America, Europe, the Middle East, Africa, the Asia Pacific, and Latin America. The company operates Dynatrace, an AI-powered observability platform, which provides solutions, including infrastructure, application, threat, and AI observability; digital experience; log analytics; application security; software delivery; and business analytics. It also offers implementation, consulting, and training services. The company markets its products through a combination of global direct sales team and a network of partners, including global system integrators (GSIs), cloud providers, resellers and technology alliance partners. It serves customers in various industries, including banking, financial services, government, insurance, retail and wholesale, transportation, and software. Dynatrace, Inc. was founded in 2005 and is headquartered in Boston, Massachusetts.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Rick M. McConnell | CEO & Director | Age 59 | Compensation: $1.4M (FY2026)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 5K people. Revenue per employee of $360K ranks in the below the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue growing 24%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $95K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $54K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (4/10).","financial_summary":["Dynatrace, Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $12.9B market cap on $2.0B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +20% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder. Operating margins are expanding by +7.3pp year-over-year, which is one of the strongest signals that the moat is deepening.","Returns on capital run at 9% against a 11% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 81% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $530M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 26 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 3.45\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 3.7% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and stock-based comp at 15% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 87% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 2 other valuation measures)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.874773241732653},{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.6% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Significant insider selling (net $2.9M)","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","dollars":-2860500.0},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Antitrust and platform-regulation risk \u2014 the larger the network effect, the larger the regulatory target on its back, and a single consent decree can reset the moat.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Gross margin tops the Technology peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here","Among the least levered in Technology \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Analyzing Dynatrace (DT) and Its Rivals","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/analyzing-dynatrace-dt-and-its-rivals.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794566731.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.754,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Dynatrace (DT) Partners With CrowdStrike And Lifts Guidance, Is It Still Below Fair Value?","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/software/nyse-dt/dynatrace/news/dynatrace-dt-partners-with-crowdstrike-and-lifts-guidance-is","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794551991.76,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.796,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["guidance"]},{"title":"Financial Contrast: LM Funding America (NASDAQ:PWCM) versus Dynatrace (NYSE:DT)","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/12/financial-contrast-lm-funding-america-nasdaqpwcm-versus-dynatrace-nysedt.html","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794500937.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.945,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"The Technical Signals Behind (DT) That Institutions Follow","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/101/The_Technical_S